  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive). Pattern: X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{亡|な}くなる (X passes away).\n\n{亡|な}くなる is the polite/euphemistic word for dying.\n\nUSAGE:\n- More polite than ⟦{死|し}ぬ→死ぬ：00669_shinu⟧\n- Used when referring to someone's death respectfully\n- Common in news reports and formal situations\n- Often used when expressing condolences\n\nKEIGO:\n- {亡|な}くなられる (honorific)\n- お{亡|な}くなり⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦なる→なる：01970_naru⟧ (more honorific)\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- ⟦{無|な}くなる→無くなる：01101_nakunaru⟧ (to disappear, to run out) - different kanji\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {亡|な}くなる: to pass away (polite)\n- ⟦{死|し}ぬ→死ぬ：00669_shinu⟧: to die (direct, can be harsh)\n- ⟦{逝|い}く→逝く：28113_iku⟧: to pass (literary)",
